# Union merge: lists of one entry a line that many PRs append to at once. Git keeps both sides' lines instead of a
# conflict, without sorting them or dropping a duplicate or a line one side deleted, so a list goes here only when a
# test compares its entries exactly and fails on such an entry. Comment lines are not all checked: one that a side
# reworded can keep its old wording next to the new. Name that test right above the list's line ("# guarded by <test>
# (<its file>)"), and rerun it after merging main. Only merges and rebases on your machine use this; GitHub's merge
# ignores it and still reports the conflict. One file a line, no patterns; scripts/test/test_gitattributes.py checks
# this block. How to merge both kinds of file here:
# docs/operations/collaboration.md, "Merging main: union-merged lists and generated files".
# guarded by TestRouteScopes (server/internal/hub/route_scopes_test.go)
server/internal/hub/testdata/route_scopes.txt merge=union
# guarded by TestHubAnswersOnlyItsOwnRoutes (server/internal/hub/architecture_guard_test.go)
server/internal/hub/testdata/hub_routes_allowed.txt merge=union
# guarded by TestHubStoreStaysSmall (server/internal/hub/architecture_guard_test.go)
server/internal/hub/testdata/hub_store_methods.txt merge=union
# guarded by test_the_list_is_sorted_unique_and_well_formed (scripts/release/test_debug_switches.py)
scripts/release/debug_switches.txt merge=union

